{"ts":"2026-10-10T11:27:51.334Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"tool","toolName":"read_files","toolCallId":"toolu_01QAPpWWTLiWKtcNWHYVktom","output":[{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\.cline-runs\\run-165739-gi16.task.md","result":"1 | # Instructions for Cline run run-165739-gi16 (mode: act, model: Cline default, started 2026-10-10T11:27:39.801Z)\n2 | \n3 | Read .clinerules and memory-bank, then do tasks/NEXT.md (T4, trimmed and time-boxed to about 60 minutes). Work in the listed order, commit when done. Run tests only after each numbered item, not after every edit.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\tasks\\NEXT.md","result":" 1 | # NEXT TASK: T4 (trimmed), guardrails, admin passcode, decoder, demo reset\n 2 | \n 3 | Time box: about 60 minutes. Feature freeze at 18:45 IST. Keep changes small; don't refactor working code.\n 4 | \n 5 | T3 reviewed: 225/225 tests and the build pass. Answers to your requests:\n 6 | - The extra `notice` and `summary` columns: **approved**.\n 7 | - Age-based payment bands: **not now**. Record them as \"Future scope\" in `memory-bank/progress.md`. Make the upper age limit **optional** in the schema only if it takes under 10 minutes; otherwise leave it.\n 8 | - Admin protection: use a simple passcode (see 1).\n 9 | \n10 | ## Do, in this order (stop and commit if time runs out)\n11 | 1. **Admin passcode:** an optional env var `ADMIN_PASSCODE` (add it to `.env.example` with no value). If it's set, every `/api/admin/*` route requires the header `x-admin-passcode`, and `/admin` shows a passcode box (kept in sessionStorage). If it's not set, `/admin` shows a visible \"Demo mode: unprotected\" banner. Add tests.\n12 | 2. **Guardrails audit**, with a test for each where possible: Aadhaar masked in UI, logs and print; no images stored; all AI output zod-validated; disclaimer footer on every report; provenance + \"verified on\" + provisional badge on every check; a fuzzy score never yields `ok`. Fix anything missing. Write the checklist and results into `tasks/LOG.md`.\n13 | 3. **Rejection decoder** `/decode` (small): a textarea (paste a rejection/status message) → `ai.ts` `classifyRejection()` → ONE code from `rejectionCodes.ts` (zod enum) + confidence → fix steps from code (Assamese + English). `UNKNOWN` or confidence < 0.7 → \"needs verification\" + what to ask at the office. Mock the AI in tests. Link it from the home page (\"Got a rejection? Decode it\").\n14 | 4. **`npm run demo:reset`:** clears `data/kaagaz.db` proposals and versions back to the built-in v1 rule packs. Make sure the home page then lists only the 3 original schemes.\n15 | 5. Small polish only if time remains: 360px-width check, loading states.\n16 | \n17 | Do NOT build: voice, letter drafting, photo upload on /decode.\n18 | \n19 | **Done when:** 1–4 work; `npm test`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint` and `npm run build` pass; LOG.md updated; committed \"T4: guardrails, admin passcode, decoder, demo reset\".","success":true}],"durationMs":14}}
