{"ts":"2026-10-10T11:27:56.784Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"tool","toolName":"read_files","toolCallId":"toolu_01U5sBKXJ7bHXiHmKFERG5jG","output":[{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\activeContext.md","result":" 1 | # Active context\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Current state (after T3)\n 4 | T3 is done: the **Rule Maintenance Agent** works end to end against the live Cline API. On `/admin` a maintainer pastes a notice or loads a demo notice. A `@cline/sdk` Agent works only through 5 tools (`getRuleSchema`, `getCurrentRule`, `proposeRule`, `runTests`, `saveProposal`), and the page shows a live tool-call log, a readable before/after diff, test results (new + regression), Publish / Reject, and version history per scheme. Published versions are live at once in `/` and `/api/check`, and the old versions are kept.\n 5 | Live run (smoke, 2026-10-10): the IGNOAPS notice gave new scheme `nsap-old-age` 1.0.0 (5/5 new tests); the Orunodoi notice gave `orunodoi-3` 2.0.0 → 2.1.0 with an Oct 1–31 2026 override (4 new + 4 regression tests pass). After publishing, `/api/check` returns 1500 on 2026-10-15 and 1250 on 2026-11-15, and the home page lists the Old Age Pension.\n 6 | 225 tests pass; typecheck, lint and build are clean.\n 7 | \n 8 | ## Decisions made in T3\n 9 | - \"Type it in\": a document counts only once its main field has a value (`MAIN_FIELD` in `docFields.ts`, `isDocAdded` / `countedDocs` in `flow.ts`). Death certificate and BPL proof (nothing is read from them) count as soon as they are added. Only counted docs go to `/api/check` and onto the cover sheet; a started-but-empty slot shows \"Type the name on the next screen to add it\".\n10 | - Code decides everything about a proposal (`rulePolicy.ts`): the version must go up; ≥ 3 new tests with unique ids; a provenance may be `verified` only if it is carried over unchanged or its `sourceUrl` appears in the notice. Otherwise it must be `provisional`, so the engine says needs_verification. `saveProposal` is refused unless every new and regression test passes. `publish` re-runs all checks (a stale proposal cannot go live).\n11 | - Regression tests = built-in suites (`schemes/regression.ts`, the \"version 1\" tests) + the tests of every published version of that scheme.\n12 | - The agent edits existing schemes with a JSON merge patch (`mergePatch.ts`, RFC 7386) instead of re-sending the whole rule (fewer tokens, faster demo).\n13 | - `ai.ts` also hosts `runToolAgent` (the agent path), so there is still one model module: it logs model / promptVersion / inputHash / toolCalls, retries once only if no tool ran yet, falls back to `{ error }`, and never throws.\n14 | - Store = `node:sqlite` file (`KAAGAZ_DB_PATH` or `data/kaagaz.db`). `rule_versions` has extra `notice` and `summary` columns (needed to re-check provenance at publish time and to show the reviewer a summary). A unique partial index allows one published row per scheme+version.\n15 | - `/` and `/admin` render per request (`connection()` inside `<Suspense>`); every request calls `syncRegistry()` (idempotent), so versions published by any process appear immediately.\n16 | - `/admin` is English-only (for maintainers, not citizens). There is no auth on `/admin`; see Requests for Claude in LOG.md.\n17 | \n18 | ## Previous state (after T2)\n19 | T2 (main flow) is done. One mobile flow on `/` (client component `src/app/_components/KaagazApp.tsx`): scheme cards (PM-KISAN first, \"flagship\") → documents (photo per slot via `/api/extract`, \"type it in\", or samples A/B/C with a purple \"Demo mode: fake sample documents\" label) → confirm fields (low confidence in amber) → big Yes/No questions → report from `/api/check`. The report shows the Eligibility banner, the Readiness banner (+ \"check at the bank\" list), Fix before you apply, Please verify, OK (collapsed), benefit (central / state top-up separately), supporting docs, a print-only cover sheet and the bilingual disclaimer. Assamese default, English toggle (`src/i18n.ts`).\n20 | 150 tests pass; typecheck, lint and build are clean. The live Cline API reads a fake Aadhaar image correctly (image input works).\n21 | \n22 | ## Decisions made in T2\n23 | - `src/server/ai.ts` is the only model caller: `extractDocument(image, hint?, deps?)` → `{ doc, detectedDocType } | { error: ai_unavailable | ai_failed | invalid_image }`, one retry, logs only model/promptVersion/inputHash/outcome. The Cline API wraps responses as `{ data: { choices } }`; both shapes are handled.\n24 | - Raw model JSON → `ExtractedDoc` in pure `src/core/extraction.ts` (full Aadhaar → last 4; unscored AI fields → 0.5 confidence so they get confirmed; non-ISO DOB → low confidence).\n25 | - Route files do NOT export `runtime = \"nodejs\"`: Next 16.4 rejects it with `cacheComponents` (Node is the default anyway). Awaiting Claude's confirmation.\n26 | - Nothing is read from the death certificate or BPL proof (presence only); `husbandName` is not collected.\n27 | - The client never imports the engine: UI helpers live in `flow.ts`, `reportView.ts`, `catalog.ts`, `thresholds.ts`; the page (a server component) passes a plain `SchemeView[]` catalog.\n28 | - \"Type it in\" adds an empty document (counted as present by the engine); flagged for Claude.\n29 | \n30 | ## Decisions made in T1\n31 | - Brief v2: **Assamese default + English**; two verdicts (eligibility, readiness); provenance on every rule (verified vs provisional).\n32 | - `RuleProvenance.sourceUrl` is nullable, but a `verified` rule must have one (schema refine). Provisional overrides from the T3 agent can start with `sourceUrl: null`.\n33 | - `ExtractedDoc.fields` is strict and only holds `aadhaarLast4` (never a full Aadhaar number). A missing per-field confidence means \"entered/confirmed by the user\"; < 0.8 → needs_verification.\n34 | - The name reference document is Aadhaar for PM-KISAN and the widow pension, and the ration card for Orunodoi.\n35 | - A PM-KISAN land-owner mismatch becomes `needs_verification` (not ok) if the user answers `land_in_family_member_name` = yes (farmer family = spouse/minor children).\n36 | - Orunodoi question ids: `nfsa_enrolled` (requirement); any-of `widow | person_with_disability | aay_card | income_below_2_lakh`; exclusions `elected_representative | professional | govt_staff_or_pensioner | contractor_or_trader | large_landholder | four_wheeler | similar_state_scheme`. All provisional.\n37 | - Widow pension: all mandatory docs (incl. `bpl_proof`) are provisional (\"commonly required; confirm locally\"); age and BPL are verified.\n38 | - The registry is in-memory: `registerScheme` validates, rejects a duplicate id+version and keeps old versions. T3 will persist versions in SQLite and register them at startup.\n39 | - Assamese strings in `labels.ts`, the scheme packs and `rejectionCodes.ts` are drafts awaiting native-speaker review (Das).\n40 | \n41 | ## Next step\n42 | T4: rejection decoder + polish. Before the demo: a phone click-through of `/` and `/admin`, native-speaker review of `src/i18n.ts` and of the Assamese text the agent writes, and a decision on protecting `/admin`.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\productContext.md","result":" 1 | # Product context: KaagazCheck (কাগজ চেক): \"Check before you apply\"\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Why it exists\n 4 | Eligible people lose welfare benefits *after* applying: names that don't match across Aadhaar, bank and land records; Aadhaar not seeded to the bank; missing certificates; rejection reasons they cannot understand. Documented example: Rajasthan 2019, only about 23% of registered PM-KISAN farmers got the 3rd instalment, mostly because of Aadhaar name mismatches (sources in `docs/research.md`).\n 5 | \n 6 | KaagazCheck checks the papers **before** the person applies, in **Assamese (default) with an English toggle**, and says exactly what to fix and where.\n 7 | **Promise:** we help catch preventable mistakes. We do NOT guarantee approval; the department decides.\n 8 | \n 9 | ## Users\n10 | - **Citizen** in Assam (farmer, widow, woman of a household) on a basic Android phone, often helped by family or a CSC/NGO helper.\n11 | - **Rule maintainer** (helper organisation) who keeps scheme rules current with the Rule Maintenance Agent (Cline SDK).\n12 | \n13 | ## Schemes in scope (rule packs v2, `docs/schemes.md` is the source of truth)\n14 | - **PM-KISAN** (`pm-kisan`): flagship end-to-end demo. No landholding-size limit.\n15 | - **Orunodoi 3.0, Assam** (`orunodoi-3`): only the ration card and ₹1,250/month are verified; everything else is provisional → \"needs verification\".\n16 | - **Widow Pension IGNWPS** (`nsap-widow`): age 40–79, BPL, central ₹300/month; state top-up unconfirmed.\n17 | \n18 | ## Main demo path (3 minutes)\n19 | 1. Pick a scheme.\n20 | 2. Add documents: photo, or \"Use sample A/B/C\" (A clean PM-KISAN, B name mismatch, C widow missing death certificate).\n21 | 3. AI reads each document → fields + confidence; low confidence → the user confirms or edits.\n22 | 4. Answer the yes/no questions.\n23 | 5. Rule engine → **two verdicts**: *Eligibility* (likely_eligible / not_eligible / needs_verification) and *Readiness* (ready_for_review / action_required / needs_verification). Each check has a reason, where to fix it, and its source (provenance, verified vs provisional).\n24 | 6. Assamese report + printable cover sheet.\n25 | \n26 | ## Cline inside the product: Rule Maintenance Agent (T3)\n27 | A scheme notice → the agent proposes a rule change (new scheme or new version, with provenance) → writes regression tests → runs them through the engine → diff + test results → a **human approves** → a new rule-pack version is published (old version kept). Demo inputs: `docs/sample-guideline-ignoaps.md` (add a scheme), `docs/sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md` (one-time ₹1,500 for October 2026, via a time-bounded benefit override).\n28 | \n29 | ## Second mode (T4)\n30 | Rejection decoder: rejection text → known reason code (`src/core/rejectionCodes.ts`) → fix steps in Assamese + English.\n31 | \n32 | ## Trust rules\n33 | - The AI only reads and explains; the rule engine decides.\n34 | - Every rule carries provenance; provisional rules and external facts (bank seeding, account active, eKYC, land verified) → needs_verification, never a definitive pass/fail.\n35 | - A fuzzy name score never equals identity: only an exact (normalised) match is `ok`.\n36 | - Aadhaar masked to the last 4 digits everywhere; images processed in memory, never stored.\n37 | - Demo uses fake sample documents only. AI-generated Assamese is labelled \"draft\"; fixed Assamese strings need native-speaker review.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\progress.md","result":" 1 | # Progress\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Done\n 4 | - [x] T0: Memory Bank, Next.js 16 scaffold (TS strict, Tailwind v4, ESLint), Vitest + fast-check + zod, npm scripts, `.gitignore`, `.env.example`, placeholder page, smoke test, first commit.\n 5 | - [x] T1: core rule engine v2. Step 0 (memory bank refreshed for brief v2; title \"KaagazCheck: কাগজ চেক\", taglines EN/AS, `<html lang=\"as\">`); zod types; 3 rule packs with provenance + versioned registry; name matcher (Devanagari + Assamese/Bengali transliteration, Jaro-Winkler); `ageOn`; `maskAadhaar`; `benefitOn` with overrides; `evaluate` with two verdicts; rejection codes EN/AS; samples A/B/C. 93 tests.\n 6 | \n 7 | - [x] T2: main flow. `src/server/ai.ts` (Cline API vision, zod, one retry, `{ error }` fallback), `/api/extract` + `/api/check`, pure helpers (`extraction`, `flow`, `reportView`, `catalog`), `src/i18n.ts` (as/en), mobile UI (scheme → docs/samples → confirm → questions → two-verdict report → print cover sheet). 150 tests.\n 8 | \n 9 | - [x] T3: \"type it in\" fix (doc counts only once its main field is filled) + Rule Maintenance Agent: `@cline/sdk` Agent with 5 zod tools, `node:sqlite` store (`rule_versions`, WAL, transactions), pure rule tests / diff / policy / merge patch, admin API (NDJSON stream, list, publish, reject), `/admin` UI (demo notices, live log, diff, tests, Publish/Reject, history), `scripts/agent-smoke.mjs`. Both demo notices verified live. 225 tests.\n10 | \n11 | ## To do\n12 | - [ ] T4: rejection decoder + polish\n13 | - [ ] T-last: freeze, full README, demo path check\n14 | \n15 | ## Known issues\n16 | - `npm install` warns that eslint@9 is deprecated (pinned by eslint-config-next 16.4.0). Harmless.\n17 | - Assamese strings (incl. all of `src/i18n.ts`) are drafts; they need native-speaker review before the demo.\n18 | - The T2 UI has not been clicked through on a real phone yet (only HTML + API smoke tests).\n19 | - Route files omit `export const runtime = \"nodejs\"` (incompatible with `cacheComponents` in Next 16.4); approved by Claude in T3.\n20 | - `/admin` has no authentication (anyone who can reach the server can run the agent and publish). Fine for the local demo; needs a decision before any deployment.\n21 | - The engine has one flat benefit amount per scheme, so IGNOAPS's ₹500/month for ages 80+ can only be a note (the agent said so itself). Age-banded benefits would need an engine change.\n22 | - A live agent run takes about 20–60 s; the UI streams each tool call so the wait is visible.\n23 | - `npm install` warns that `protobufjs` (a dependency of `@cline/sdk`) has an unapproved postinstall script. Harmless; nothing is broken.\n24 | - The transliteration table is basic (good enough for possible_match on common names; cross-script is never `same`).","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\projectbrief.md","result":" 1 | # Project brief v2: KaagazCheck (কাগজ চেক): \"Check before you apply\"\n 2 | \n 3 | **Pitch:** We help citizens catch preventable welfare-application mistakes *before* they submit their papers. Our AI reads the documents; a tested rule engine checks them; and Cline maintains the rules as official guidelines change.\n 4 | **Promise:** we reduce preventable errors. We do NOT guarantee approval; the department decides.\n 5 | \n 6 | ## Problem (evidence: docs/research.md)\n 7 | Eligible people lose benefits after applying because their documents disagree (name spellings across Aadhaar, bank and land record; account not Aadhaar-seeded; missing papers) or because rejections arrive unexplained. In Rajasthan in 2019, only about 23% of registered PM-KISAN farmers got the third instalment, mostly due to name mismatches with Aadhaar.\n 8 | \n 9 | ## Users\n10 | - **Citizen** in Assam on a basic Android phone, often helped by family or a CSC/NGO helper.\n11 | - **Rule maintainer** (helper organisation) who keeps scheme rules current using the Cline agent.\n12 | \n13 | ## Languages\n14 | **Assamese (default) + English toggle.** All fixed UI and check messages live in one `src/i18n.ts` with `as` and `en` keys. Assamese strings must be reviewed by a native speaker before the demo (Das will arrange). AI-generated Assamese (letters, explanations) is labelled \"draft\".\n15 | \n16 | ## Scope: rule packs v2 (docs/schemes.md is the source of truth)\n17 | - **PM-KISAN: flagship, full end-to-end demo** (name mismatch, missing document, uncertain bank status).\n18 | - **Orunodoi 3.0: Assam relevance, verified rules only;** provisional criteria → \"needs verification\".\n19 | - **Widow Pension (IGNWPS): simple, reliable rules** (age 40–79, BPL, central ₹300/month).\n20 | \n21 | ## Architecture (the trust design)\n22 | 1. **Document reader (AI):** extracts names, dates, account details and document type, with per-field confidence. Low confidence → user confirms.\n23 | 2. **Deterministic rule engine (pure code, tested):** normalises fields, checks consistency, evaluates verified criteria, finds missing documents. Provisional rules and external facts → `needs_verification`.\n24 | 3. **Two separate verdicts:** *Eligibility* (likely_eligible / not_eligible / needs_verification) and *Readiness* (ready_for_review / action_required / needs_verification).\n25 | 4. **Next steps:** corrections, where to go (bank, Aadhaar centre, circle office, Gram Panchayat), the source of each rule, and a printable cover sheet.\n26 | 5. **Explainer (AI, optional):** friendly wording in Assamese, built only from the engine's result.\n27 | \n28 | ## Core loop (must-ship demo path)\n29 | Pick scheme → add documents (photo, or \"Use sample A/B/C\") → confirm low-confidence fields → answer yes/no questions → two-verdict report with fixes and sources → print cover sheet.\n30 | Samples (clearly fake): A = clean PM-KISAN farmer → ready_for_review (+ bank seeding needs verification). B = PM-KISAN with \"RAMESH KR SHARMA\" (bank, possible match) and \"Rameshwar Sharma\" (land record, mismatch) → action_required. C = widow pension, missing death certificate → action_required.\n31 | \n32 | ## Cline inside the product: Rule Maintenance Agent (T3)\n33 | Upload or paste a scheme notice → a `@cline/sdk` Agent proposes a **rule change** (new scheme or edited rule, with provenance: sourceUrl, clause, effectiveDate) → writes **regression tests** → runs them through the engine (existing scheme tests must still pass) → shows a diff + test results → a **human approves** → a new rule-pack version is published (old version kept). Demo inputs: `docs/sample-guideline-ignoaps.md` (add a scheme) and `docs/sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md` (a one-time payment change, to show versioning).\n34 | \n35 | ## Trust rules (non-negotiable)\n36 | - AI reads and explains; **code decides**. No eligibility claim from model text.\n37 | - Aadhaar masked to the last 4 digits everywhere; images processed in memory, never stored.\n38 | - Every rule carries provenance; provisional → needs_verification.\n39 | - A fuzzy name score never equals identity.\n40 | - Demo uses fake documents only.\n41 | \n42 | ## Data model sketch\n43 | - `RuleProvenance` { sourceUrl, sourceTitle, clause?, effectiveDate?, verifiedOn, version, status: verified | provisional }\n44 | - `SchemeRule` { id, version, nameEn, nameAs, benefit { centralShare, stateTopUp|null, period, effectiveDate, provenance }, mandatoryDocs[], supportingDocs[], ageRange?, eligibilityAnyOf[], exclusions[], externalChecks[], each criterion with provenance }\n45 | - `ExtractedDoc` { docType, fields { name, dob, aadhaarLast4, accountNo, ifsc, ownerNames[], husbandName, ... }, confidence per field }\n46 | - `Report` { eligibility, readiness, checks[], schemeVersion, asOfDate }\n47 | - DB (T3): `rule_versions` { schemeId, version, ruleJson, testsJson, testResultJson, status: proposed | published | rejected, sourceNote, createdAt, approvedAt }\n48 | \n49 | ## Stretch\n50 | Assamese voice readout (only if the browser has an as-IN voice; otherwise hide) · rejection-notice decoder (T4) · helper mode for many applicants.\n51 | \n52 | ## Cut list (cut in this order)\n53 | Voice → decoder letter drafting → real photo upload (keep samples + manual entry) → cover-sheet styling. **Never cut:** the two-verdict report, provenance, the Cline agent with tests + approval.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\systemPatterns.md","result":" 1 | # System patterns\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Core pipeline: AI reads → rule engine decides → AI explains\n 4 | 1. **Read (AI):** a document image or text → `ExtractedDoc` (fields + per-field confidence), validated with zod.\n 5 | 2. **Decide (pure code):** `evaluate(scheme, docs, answers, asOfDate) → Report` in `src/core/evaluate.ts`. Deterministic, unit- and property-tested. No model text ever decides a status.\n 6 | 3. **Explain (AI, optional):** friendlier Assamese wording or a letter draft, built only from the report's checks (labelled \"draft\").\n 7 | \n 8 | ## Module boundaries\n 9 | - `src/core/`: pure TypeScript. No React, network, DB, `process.env` or implicit \"today\" (`asOfDate` is always passed in).\n10 |   - `types.ts` zod schemas: `RuleProvenance`, `SchemeRule` (versioned), `ExtractedDoc`, `Answers`, `Check`, `Report`, `BenefitOn`.\n11 |   - `schemes/` rule packs (`pm-kisan.ts`, `orunodoi-3.ts`, `nsap-widow.ts`; provenance helpers in `sources.ts`) + registry `index.ts`: `getScheme(id, version?)`, `listSchemes()`, `listSchemeVersions(id)`, `registerScheme(rule)` (validates; keeps old versions; newest wins), `questionsFor(scheme)`.\n12 |   - `nameMatch.ts` (+ `transliterate.ts`), `age.ts` (`ageOn`), `aadhaar.ts` (`maskAadhaar`), `benefit.ts` (`benefitOn` with time-bounded overrides), `rejectionCodes.ts`, `labels.ts` (bilingual doc/office labels, disclaimer), `samples.ts` (fake sample sets A/B/C), `dates.ts`.\n13 |   - T2 UI helpers (pure, client-safe; they don't import the engine): `extraction.ts` (raw model JSON → `ExtractedDoc`), `docFields.ts`, `flow.ts`, `reportView.ts` (sections/tones/₹ formatting), `catalog.ts` (`SchemeView`), `thresholds.ts`.\n14 | - `src/i18n.ts` (T2): every fixed UI string in `as` + `en` (same keys, tested); reuses `labels.ts`.\n15 | - `src/server/ai.ts` (T2): the **only** module that calls a model. Structured JSON → zod → one retry → safe fallback `{ error }`. Logs model, prompt version, input hash (never raw personal data). `fetch`/`env`/`log` are injectable for tests.\n16 | - `src/server/api.ts` (T2): request schemas + handlers for `/api/check` (engine only) and `/api/extract` (via ai.ts); the route files are thin wrappers.\n17 | - `src/app/_components/` (T2): the single client flow `KaagazApp` and its steps; `page.tsx` (server) passes a plain catalog + samples.\n18 | - T3 pure core: `ruleTests.ts` (zod `RuleTestCase` benefit|evaluate + deterministic `runRuleTests`), `schemes/regression.ts` (built-in regression suites), `ruleDiff.ts` (keyed before/after diff), `ruleDiffView.ts` (plain-English labels for the UI), `rulePolicy.ts` (version bump, ≥ 3 new tests, verified-provenance rule), `mergePatch.ts` (RFC 7386), `notice.ts` (normalise; extract the demo notices), `agentLog.ts` (one-line tool summaries).\n19 | - `src/server/store.ts` (T3): the **only** database writer (`node:sqlite`, WAL, every write in `BEGIN IMMEDIATE … COMMIT`); `rule_versions` table (+ `notice`, `summary`).\n20 | - `src/server/rules.ts` (T3): `RuleService`: candidate (full rule or merge patch) → validate (zod + policy) → runTests (new + regression) → saveProposal (only if all pass) → publish (re-check, then `registerScheme`) / reject. `syncRegistry()` loads published versions into the registry (idempotent; called per request).\n21 | - `src/server/agents/ruleMaintenance.ts` (T3): `@cline/sdk` Rule Maintenance Agent: system prompt + 5 `createTool` tools (zod inputs, re-validated with `checked()`), session state, `runRuleAgent(notice)` → streams `AgentEvent`s; the result comes from what was saved through the tools, never from the agent's text.\n22 | - `src/server/ai.ts` also has `runToolAgent` (Cline SDK `Agent`, `openai-compatible` → Cline API): it is still the only module that talks to a model.\n23 | - `src/server/adminApi.ts` + `src/app/api/admin/rules/**` (T3): propose (NDJSON stream), list (history + diff), `[id]/publish`, `[id]/reject`. `src/app/admin/` is the maintainer UI.\n24 | - `src/app/api/**/route.ts`: thin handlers on the Node.js runtime (the default; an explicit `runtime` export breaks the build with `cacheComponents`).\n25 | - `src/app/**`: UI (Assamese default, English toggle; fixed strings in `src/i18n.ts`). Calls API routes, never the model.\n26 | \n27 | ## Result model (docs/schemes.md v2)\n28 | - Check result: `ok | action_required | needs_verification | not_applicable`; kind: `document | name | field | eligibility | external`. Every check has `messageEn`, `messageAs`, `fixWhere`, `provenance`, plus `match` for name checks.\n29 | - **Eligibility:** `not_eligible` only when a **verified** eligibility criterion failed; any provisional, unanswered or unreadable criterion → `needs_verification`; else `likely_eligible`.\n30 | - **Readiness:** any `action_required` (missing mandatory doc, name `mismatch`, bad IFSC/account format, failed verified criterion) → `action_required`; else any non-external `needs_verification` (possible match, initials, low confidence, provisional) → `needs_verification`; else `ready_for_review`. External checks (bank seeding, account active, eKYC, land verified, ration card active) are always `needs_verification` and listed, but on their own they don't block `ready_for_review`.\n31 | - Money: `centralShare` + `stateTopUp` (null = unconfirmed → `total` null; never show an unconfirmed total). Overrides are inclusive date windows; the last matching one wins.\n32 | \n33 | ## Name matching (showcase, defensive)\n34 | Tokenise → drop leading honorifics (SHRI/SMT/MR/MRS/KUMARI/LATE…) → transliterate Devanagari/Assamese/Bengali → canonical variants (KR→KUMAR, MD/MOHD→MOHAMMAD, DEBI→DEVI, SK→SHEIKH…). Levels: `same` (identical after formatting; the only level that gives `ok`), `possible_match` (variants, transliteration, word order, or every word pair Jaro-Winkler ≥ 0.85), `initials_only`, `mismatch` (incl. a missing/extra word). The score is shown but never decides.\n35 | \n36 | ## Privacy\n37 | Aadhaar: only `aadhaarLast4` is stored in `ExtractedDoc`; `maskAadhaar` → `XXXX XXXX 1234`. Images processed in memory only. Minimum personal data.\n38 | \n39 | ## Testing\n40 | Vitest + fast-check, tests first for core logic. Properties: name same-as-itself, symmetry, mask ≤ 4 digits, possible_match never `ok`, Orunodoi never `not_eligible`, evaluate deterministic + schema-valid, readiness invariant.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\techContext.md","result":" 1 | # Tech context\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Stack\n 4 | - One Next.js 16 app (App Router, `src/` dir, `@/*` → `./src/*`), React 19, TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS v4 (via `@tailwindcss/turbopack` loader in `next.config.ts`).\n 5 | - Validation: zod 4.\n 6 | - Tests: Vitest 5 (Node environment, `src/**/*.test.ts`) + fast-check 4.\n 7 | - Lint: ESLint 9 flat config (`eslint-config-next`); `next lint` no longer exists in Next 16.\n 8 | - Database (T3, done): built-in `node:sqlite` (WAL, SQLite 3.53.4) in `src/server/store.ts`; no fallback needed.\n 9 | - AI: Cline API (OpenAI-compatible), base URL `https://api.cline.bot/api/v1`, all calls via `src/server/ai.ts`.\n10 | - In-product agent (T3, done): `@cline/sdk@0.0.92` `Agent`, `providerId: \"openai-compatible\"`, tools via `createTool` with zod schemas (details below).\n11 | \n12 | ## Environment\n13 | - Windows, PowerShell 5.1; the path contains a space (`C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build`). Use npm scripts and cross-platform Node code.\n14 | - Node v24.21.0, npm 11.19.0, git 2.55.0.\n15 | - Secrets only in `.env.local` (git-ignored): `CLINE_API_KEY`, `CLINE_MODEL` (e.g. `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5`, never a `:batch` model). The template is `.env.example`.\n16 | - Write files containing Assamese (or other non-Latin text) with the editor tool (UTF-8), not PowerShell redirection. Assamese uses ৰ (U+09F0) and ৱ (U+09F1), not Bengali র/ব.\n17 | - The editor tool rejects payloads over ~6000 characters: write large files in chunks (create, then insert at the end).\n18 | - `tsconfig.json` includes `**/*.ts`, so never leave scratch `.ts` files in the repo root while running `next build`.\n19 | \n20 | ## npm scripts\n21 | | Script | Command |\n22 | |---|---|\n23 | | `dev` | `next dev` |\n24 | | `build` | `next build` |\n25 | | `start` | `next start` |\n26 | | `lint` | `eslint .` |\n27 | | `typecheck` | `tsc --noEmit` |\n28 | | `test` | `vitest run` |\n29 | | `test:watch` | `vitest` |\n30 | \n31 | ## Gotchas found in T0\n32 | - Vitest 5 needs `@types/node` ≥ 22 (peer dep), so `@types/node` is `^22`.\n33 | - The Vitest config is `vitest.config.mts` (ESM); a `.ts` config triggers a Vite \"configLoader native\" warning because `package.json` has no `\"type\": \"module\"`.\n34 | - The global `LayoutProps<\"/\">` type only exists after `next build`/`next dev` generate `.next/types`, so `layout.tsx` uses an explicit `Readonly<{ children: React.ReactNode }>` to keep `npm run typecheck` working on a clean checkout.\n35 | - Vite writes warnings to stderr, which PowerShell reports as `NativeCommandError`. Check the real exit code (e.g. run via `cmd /c ... & echo %ERRORLEVEL%`).\n36 | - `npm install` is slow here (about 5 minutes for a fresh install); long commands can exceed the tool timeout, so run them in the background with logs.\n37 | \n38 | ## Gotchas found in T2\n39 | - Next 16.4 + `cacheComponents: true` **rejects `export const runtime = \"nodejs\"`** in route files (build error). Node.js is the default runtime, so routes omit it.\n40 | - The Cline API (`/chat/completions`) returns the OpenAI body wrapped as `{ data: { choices: [...] } }`. Image input (`image_url` data URL) works with `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5`.\n41 | - This PowerShell session had an **empty `CLINE_MODEL` env var** set. Next never overrides an existing env var from `.env.local`, so the AI looked unconfigured. Run `Remove-Item Env:CLINE_MODEL` before `next dev`/`next start` if `/api/extract` says `ai_unavailable` while `.env.local` is filled.\n42 | - In Vitest, `beforeEach(() => mock.mockReset())` returns the mock, which Vitest then runs as a teardown. Use a block body `beforeEach(() => { mock.mockReset(); })`.\n43 | - Manual smoke test: `npm run build`, `npx next start -p 3123`, `node scripts/smoke.mjs http://localhost:3123`.\n44 | \n45 | ## Cline SDK (`@cline/sdk` 0.0.92), found in T3 by reading node_modules\n46 | - `@cline/sdk` is only `export * from \"@cline/core\"`. Core re-exports `Agent` (from `@cline/agents`, same class as `AgentRuntime`) and `createTool` (from `@cline/shared`). ESM-only, Node ≥ 22, depends on zod ^4.\n47 | - `new Agent({ providerId: \"openai-compatible\", baseUrl: \"https://api.cline.bot/api/v1\", apiKey, modelId, systemPrompt, tools, maxIterations, toolExecution })` → `agent.run(text)` returns `{ status: \"completed\"|\"aborted\"|\"failed\", outputText, iterations, usage, error? }`. `agent.subscribe(fn)` streams events: `tool-started` / `tool-finished` (`toolCall { toolCallId, toolName, input }`, `message.content[].output`), `assistant-text-delta` (`accumulatedText`), `run-failed`, etc. `agent.abort()` cancels.\n48 | - `createTool({ name, description, inputSchema: zodSchema, execute })` converts zod → JSON Schema (`additionalProperties: false`). It does **not** zod-validate the input before `execute` (verified: `{a: 5}` reached a `z.string()` tool), so each tool wraps `execute` in `checked(schema, fn)` → `safeParse` → `{ error }`. Default tool timeout 30 s, retryable, max 3 retries.\n49 | - The agent retries transient provider errors itself. A thrown `execute` error becomes an `isError` tool result the model sees.\n50 | - Matches .clinerules/03-stack.md; no differences in the API used.\n51 | - **Turbopack cannot bundle `@cline/core`** (dynamic `new URL(\"./entry.\"+ext, import.meta.url)` worker URLs → 72 \"Module not found\" errors). Fixed with `serverExternalPackages: [\"@cline/sdk\", \"@cline/core\", \"@cline/agents\", \"@cline/llms\", \"@cline/shared\"]` in `next.config.ts`.\n52 | - `ai.ts` imports `@cline/sdk` lazily (dynamic import) inside the real agent factory; `ruleMaintenance.ts` imports `createTool` statically (cold import ≈ 1.4 s, only on admin routes).\n53 | - Live timing with `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5`: Orunodoi notice ≈ 21 s (6 tool calls), IGNOAPS new scheme ≈ 30–60 s. Longer than the tool timeout here, so run `scripts/agent-smoke.mjs` in the background with a log.\n54 | \n55 | ## T3 storage\n56 | - `node:sqlite` works inside Next 16 route handlers and Vitest (no build trouble). DB file: `KAAGAZ_DB_PATH` or `data/kaagaz.db` (`/data/` is git-ignored). Vitest sets `KAAGAZ_DB_PATH=:memory:` (vitest.config.mts), so tests never touch `data/`.\n57 | - A page that reads the DB/registry per request needs `await connection()` inside a `<Suspense>` child (Cache Components). `connection()` throws outside a Next request scope, so unit tests call the handler (`handleList`) instead of the route.\n58 | - `cmd /c \"x & echo %ERRORLEVEL%\"` expands ERRORLEVEL too early (prints empty). Use `cmd /c \"npm test >nul 2>&1\"; $LASTEXITCODE` in PowerShell.\n59 | \n60 | ## Scaffold notes\n61 | Generated with `create-next-app@16.4.0` in a temp folder and copied in (it refuses non-empty folders). Defaults kept: `cacheComponents: true`, `partialPrefetching: true`. `AGENTS.md` is written by Next (`next dev` re-adds it), so it is committed.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\tasks\\backlog\\T4-decoder-polish.md","result":" 1 | # T4: Rejection decoder, guardrails, polish (about 75 min)\n 2 | \n 3 | Mode: ACT. Cut from the bottom if time is short.\n 4 | \n 5 | 1. **Guardrails audit (do first):** Aadhaar masked in UI, logs and print; no images stored; every AI output zod-validated; footer disclaimer on every report; provenance + \"verified on\" + provisional badge on every check; no check turns `ok` from a fuzzy score.\n 6 | 2. **Rejection decoder** (`/decode`): paste text or a photo of a rejection/status message → `ai.ts` `classifyRejection()` returns ONE code from `rejectionCodes.ts` + confidence; fix steps come from code (Assamese + English). UNKNOWN or low confidence → \"needs verification\" + what to ask at the office.\n 7 | 3. Draft a correction/grievance letter (AI, Assamese, labelled \"draft, please check\") on the print page.\n 8 | 4. Voice: 🔊 read the report aloud only if the browser has an Assamese (as-IN) voice; otherwise hide the button (don't fall back to a wrong language).\n 9 | 5. `npm run demo:reset`: clears proposals, restores v1 rule packs, seeds samples.\n10 | 6. Polish: big tap targets, loading/empty/error states, works at 360px width.\n11 | \n12 | **Done when:** \"Payment failed: Aadhaar not seeded with bank account\" → `AADHAAR_NOT_SEEDED_BANK` with Assamese fix steps; guardrails verified; tests + build pass; committed \"T4: decoder, guardrails, polish\".","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\docs\\PS.md","result":" 1 | # Cline AI Builder Hackathon: Round 2 Problem Statement\n 2 | \n 3 | India has problems that millions of people live with every day. What would you build with AI to solve one of them?\n 4 | \n 5 | India is building at a scale few countries have ever attempted, yet for hundreds of millions of people daily life still runs into the same walls. A farmer cannot tell what is wrong with his crop until the damage is done. A patient from a small town travels for hours to meet a doctor who has only a few minutes to give her. A student studies from notes written in a language she does not think in. A citizen loses months to a government scheme he qualified for but never heard about.\n 6 | \n 7 | These are not rare cases. They repeat across healthcare, education, agriculture, governance, finance, safety and climate, and across languages, incomes and literacy levels. AI can finally make a real dent: it understands Indian languages and voice, reads messy documents, reasons over local data and can reach anyone with a basic smartphone.\n 8 | \n 9 | **The challenge:** pick one real problem that Indian society faces and, in 8 hours, build an AI-powered solution for it, using Cline as your AI coding partner from the first commit to the last. You can also build Cline into the solution itself, for example with the Cline SDK. Not a slide deck, but a working product that a real person could use tomorrow.\n10 | \n11 | The problem is yours to choose. Healthcare, education, agriculture, governance, finance, safety and climate are only some examples, so look at the problems around you and pick one that matters. For example, potholes are a problem on roads across India, and one solution is a dashcam in a car with AI that spots potholes as it drives and prepares the complaint automatically.\n12 | \n13 | ## Deliverables\n14 | - **Codebase on GitHub (with README):** a public repository with a clear README covering the problem, your solution, architecture, tech stack, setup steps and how Cline was used in the build.\n15 | - **PPT:** a presentation covering the problem, your solution, the architecture, the AI models and tools involved, how Cline was used (in the build and inside the solution), challenges faced and future scope.\n16 | - **Demo video (mandatory):** a short walkthrough of your working solution with a real user scenario, showing Cline in action during the build.\n17 | - **Social media post (brownie points):** share your build, demo, experience or participation shoutout, and tag Cline.\n18 | \n19 | ## Evaluation criteria\n20 | Creativity & uniqueness · Innovation · Real-world usefulness · Effective use of Cline · Product usability & overall execution · Technical implementation. **Bonus** for solutions that use Cline inside the product itself, not only to build it.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\tasks\\LOG.md","result":"  1 | # Build log (Cline appends after every task)\n  2 | \n  3 | ## T0: scaffold + memory bank (run-133358-c1ef, 2026-10-10)\n  4 | Followed the plan from run-133031-4cma.\n  5 | \n  6 | **Files created/changed**\n  7 | - Memory Bank: `memory-bank/productContext.md`, `systemPatterns.md`, `techContext.md`, `activeContext.md`, `progress.md` (`projectbrief.md` untouched).\n  8 | - Scaffold (create-next-app@16.4.0 in a temp folder, copied in): `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `tsconfig.json` (strict), `next.config.ts`, `eslint.config.mjs` (+ ignores for `.cline-runs/`, `docs/`, `memory-bank/`, `tasks/`), `next-env.d.ts`, `AGENTS.md`, `public/*`, `src/app/{layout.tsx,page.tsx,globals.css,favicon.ico}`.\n  9 | - New: `src/core/appInfo.ts` (title/taglines, pure), `src/core/appInfo.test.ts` (smoke test, also exercises zod + fast-check), `vitest.config.mts`, `.env.example` (`CLINE_API_KEY=`, `CLINE_MODEL=`), `README.md` (short placeholder), `.gitignore` (ignores `.env`, `.env*.local`, `node_modules`, `.next`, `*.db*`; keeps `.env.example` and `.cline-runs/`).\n 10 | - Deps added: `zod@^4.6.5`, dev `vitest@^5.0.3`, `fast-check@^4.10.2`, `@types/node@^22`.\n 11 | - Scripts: `dev`, `build`, `start`, `lint` (`eslint .`), `typecheck` (`tsc --noEmit`), `test` (`vitest run`), `test:watch`.\n 12 | \n 13 | **Results**\n 14 | - `npm test`: 1 file, 3 passed, 0 failed.\n 15 | - `npm run typecheck`: pass. `npm run lint`: pass (0 problems). `npm run build`: pass (Next 16.4.0, Turbopack; `/` prerendered static).\n 16 | - Verified the built HTML contains \"KaagazCheck: कागज़ चेक\" and `lang=\"hi\"`, and the CSS contains the Tailwind utilities used.\n 17 | \n 18 | **Deviations from the plan**\n 19 | - `@types/node` bumped from `^20` to `^22` (Vitest 5 peer requirement; matches Node 22+).\n 20 | - Vitest config is `.mts` instead of `.ts` (avoids a Vite ESM/CJS config warning).\n 21 | - `layout.tsx` uses explicit `Readonly<{ children: React.ReactNode }>` instead of the generated global `LayoutProps<\"/\">`, so `typecheck` passes before `.next/types` exists.\n 22 | - No `postcss.config.mjs`: create-next-app 16.4 wires Tailwind v4 via the `@tailwindcss/turbopack` loader in `next.config.ts`; Tailwind confirmed working in the build.\n 23 | \n 24 | **Open issues**\n 25 | - npm warns `eslint@9` is deprecated (pinned by eslint-config-next 16.4.0) and that `unrs-resolver` has an unapproved postinstall script; neither blocks lint or build.\n 26 | - `docs/sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md` appeared in `docs/` during this run (not created by Cline); committed as-is with `git add -A`.\n 27 | \n 28 | **Requests for Claude**\n 29 | - None blocking. Please confirm that `docs/sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md` is intended for T4 (rejection decoder) and reference it in the task spec if so.\n 30 | \n 31 | ## T1: core rule engine v2 (run-134715-f3yl, 2026-10-10)\n 32 | Followed `tasks/NEXT.md` (Step 0 + `tasks/backlog/T1-core-engine.md`), with `docs/schemes.md` v2 as the source of truth. I wrote the tests first: all new test files were written before the implementations, and the Step 0 smoke tests failed until `appInfo.ts` was updated.\n 33 | \n 34 | **Step 0**\n 35 | - Memory bank: `productContext.md`, `systemPatterns.md`, `activeContext.md` rewritten for brief v2 (two verdicts, provenance, Assamese). `progress.md` and `techContext.md` updated.\n 36 | - `src/core/appInfo.ts`: `APP_TITLE` \"KaagazCheck: কাগজ চেক\", `APP_TAGLINE_EN` \"Check before you apply\", `APP_TAGLINE_AS` \"আবেদনৰ আগতে পৰীক্ষা কৰক\", `APP_LANG = \"as\"`, and a longer `APP_DESCRIPTION_EN` for meta. `layout.tsx` uses `lang={APP_LANG}`; `page.tsx` shows the Assamese tagline first. The smoke test checks the exact title and taglines, Assamese ৰ (U+09F0) rather than Bengali র, and `lang`.\n 37 | \n 38 | **Files created (all pure, in `src/core/`)**\n 39 | - `types.ts`: zod schemas `RuleProvenance`, `SchemeRule` (with `version`), `ExtractedDoc`, `Answers`, `Question`, `DocRequirement`, `NameCheckRule`, `FieldCheckRule`, `ExternalCheckRule`, `AgeRange`, `Benefit` (+ `BenefitOverride`), `Check`, `Report`, `BenefitOn`.\n 40 | - `schemes/sources.ts` (provenance builders, verifiedOn 2026-10-10), `schemes/pm-kisan.ts`, `schemes/orunodoi-3.ts`, `schemes/nsap-widow.ts`, `schemes/index.ts` (`getScheme`, `listSchemes`, `listSchemeVersions`, `registerScheme`, `questionsFor`).\n 41 | - `nameMatch.ts` (+ `transliterate.ts`: Devanagari and Assamese/Bengali → Latin), `age.ts`, `aadhaar.ts`, `benefit.ts`, `evaluate.ts`, `rejectionCodes.ts`, `labels.ts`, `samples.ts` (fake samples A/B/C), `dates.ts`.\n 42 | - Tests: `nameMatch.test.ts`, `age.test.ts`, `aadhaar.test.ts`, `benefit.test.ts`, `evaluate.test.ts`, `rejectionCodes.test.ts`, `schemes/schemes.test.ts`.\n 43 | \n 44 | **Results**\n 45 | - `npm test`: 8 files, **93 passed, 0 failed** (including fast-check properties: same-as-itself, symmetry, mask ≤ 4 digits, possible_match never ok, Orunodoi never not_eligible, deterministic + schema-valid report, readiness invariant).\n 46 | - `npm run typecheck`: pass. `npm run lint`: pass. `npm run build`: pass. The built HTML has `lang=\"as\"`, the Assamese title and both taglines, and no Devanagari.\n 47 | - Required name cases and their scores: same (1) / same (1) / possible_match (0.999) / possible_match (0.999) / initials_only (0.875) / mismatch (0.644) / mismatch (0.778).\n 48 | - Samples on 2026-10-10: A → likely_eligible + ready_for_review (4 external checks need verification). B → action_required (bank possible_match, land mismatch). C → action_required (death certificate missing).\n 49 | \n 50 | **Design decisions / interpretations (please review)**\n 51 | - **Readiness with external checks:** external checks are always `needs_verification` but do not by themselves stop `ready_for_review`. This is needed for the T1 spec \"clean → ready_for_review with bank seeding as needs_verification\". Any other `needs_verification` (possible match, initials, low confidence < 0.8, provisional criterion, unanswered question) → readiness `needs_verification`.\n 52 | - **A verified criterion that fails** (e.g. income tax payer) → eligibility `not_eligible` and readiness `action_required`.\n 53 | - **Name `same`** means identical after formatting (case, punctuation, spaces, joined words, leading honorifics), compared in the original script. Any cross-script comparison is at best `possible_match`. The score is capped at 0.999 for anything that is not `same`. `possible_match` also covers reordered words and \"every word pair Jaro-Winkler ≥ 0.85\". A missing or extra word is a `mismatch` (so \"Rameshwar Sharma\" vs \"Ramesh Kumar Sharma\" is a mismatch).\n 54 | - **Honorifics** are dropped only when they lead the name, so \"Sunita Kumari\" keeps KUMARI as a surname.\n 55 | - **PM-KISAN land owner:** a mismatch becomes `needs_verification` (never ok) if the user answers `land_in_family_member_name` = yes. docs/schemes.md allows \"applicant (or a family member) as owner\". The relationship can't be proven from a photo.\n 56 | - **Orunodoi** name checks use the ration card as the reference. Provisional questions are `nfsa_enrolled`, an any-of list and 7 exclusions. \"None of the any-of conditions\" → `needs_verification`. `ration_card_valid` is an external check.\n 57 | - **Widow pension** mandatory docs include `bpl_proof`, all provisional (docs/schemes.md: \"commonly required; confirm locally\"). A DOB that is low-confidence, unreadable or missing → age `needs_verification`, never `not_eligible`.\n 58 | - `RuleProvenance.sourceUrl` is nullable for provisional rules (needed for the T3 Orunodoi override \"provisional until an official notice URL is added\"). A schema refine stops a `verified` rule from having a null URL.\n 59 | - `benefitOn`: overrides are inclusive date windows and the last match wins. `total` is null when `stateTopUp` is null.\n 60 | - The registry is in-memory and keeps old versions. `getScheme(id)` returns the newest version; `getScheme(id, version)` returns that version.\n 61 | \n 62 | **Open issues**\n 63 | - All Assamese strings (scheme questions, labels, check messages, rejection fix steps, tagline) are drafts and need native-speaker review (Das).\n 64 | - The transliteration table is basic (no conjunct special cases beyond virama; schwa deletion only at word end).\n 65 | - The registry test registers `nsap-widow@2.1.0` in the shared in-memory registry. Vitest isolates test files, so other files are unaffected.\n 66 | \n 67 | **Requests for Claude**\n 68 | - Please confirm the readiness rule for external checks (they don't block `ready_for_review` on their own), or say if you want a different label, e.g. `ready_for_review` with a \"confirm these N items\" list. T2's UI will show them as a separate \"confirm at bank/portal\" group.\n 69 | - Please confirm the Orunodoi any-of list and the widow pension `bpl_proof` document are wanted as modelled.\n 70 | \n 71 | \n 72 | ## T2: main flow (run-144641-b8cr, 2026-10-10)\n 73 | Followed `tasks/NEXT.md` (T2 + adjustments) and `tasks/backlog/T2-main-flow.md`. I wrote tests first for every new pure module and for both API routes. One mobile flow: scheme → documents → confirm fields → questions → two-verdict report → print cover sheet.\n 74 | \n 75 | **Files created**\n 76 | - Pure core (tested): `src/core/extraction.ts` (raw model JSON → strict `ExtractedDoc`; DD/MM/YYYY → ISO; full Aadhaar → last 4 digits; AI-read fields without a score get confidence 0.5 so they are always confirmed), `src/core/docFields.ts` (which fields each doc type needs), `src/core/flow.ts` (document slots, field edit/confirm, upsert/remove, relevant answers), `src/core/reportView.ts` (fix / verify / external / ok sections, 🟢🔴🟡⚪ tones, `₹1,25,000` formatting, benefit view), `src/core/catalog.ts` (serialisable scheme list, PM-KISAN first as flagship), `src/core/thresholds.ts`.\n 77 | - `src/i18n.ts`: all fixed UI strings, `as` (default) + `en`, same keys (tested), with doc/office names reused from `labels.ts`.\n 78 | - `src/server/ai.ts`: the only model caller. Cline API chat/completions with an `image_url` part, then JSON extraction, zod `RawExtraction`, `toExtractedDoc`, one retry, then `{ error }` (`ai_unavailable` | `ai_failed` | `invalid_image`). `fetch`/`env`/`log` are injectable for tests. Logs `{ model, promptVersion: \"extract-doc-v1\", inputHash (sha256/16), attempt, outcome, ms }` only.\n 79 | - `src/server/api.ts` + `src/app/api/check/route.ts`, `src/app/api/extract/route.ts` (thin). `/api/check` validates with zod (strict `ExtractedDoc`, so a full Aadhaar is rejected), 404 for an unknown scheme/version, `asOfDate` defaults to today in IST. Error bodies hold only paths and codes, never submitted values.\n 80 | - UI (`src/app/_components/`): `KaagazApp` (state + steps), `SchemeStep`, `DocsStep` (photo per slot with camera capture, browser downscale to JPEG ≤1600px, \"type it in\", samples A/B/C for the chosen scheme), `ConfirmStep` (low confidence highlighted in amber, \"This is correct\" button), `QuestionsStep` (big Yes/No, \"rule not confirmed\" badge), `ReportStep` + `CheckItem` + `BenefitCard`, `CoverSheet` (print only, masked Aadhaar, no account number), `ui.tsx`, `image.ts`.\n 81 | - `scripts/smoke.mjs`: manual smoke test against a running server (not part of `npm test`).\n 82 | - Tests: `src/core/{extraction,flow,reportView,catalog}.test.ts`, `src/i18n.test.ts`, `src/server/{ai,apiCheck,apiExtract}.test.ts` (ai.ts mocked in the API tests; `fetch` injected in the ai tests; no network).\n 83 | \n 84 | **Files changed**\n 85 | - `src/app/page.tsx` (server component → `KaagazApp` with the catalog + samples), `src/app/layout.tsx` (Noto Sans Bengali for Assamese, viewport, Geist Mono dropped), `src/app/globals.css` (one light high-contrast theme, font stack, print background).\n 86 | - `src/core/evaluate.ts`: `LOW_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD` moved to `thresholds.ts` and re-exported, so the client bundle doesn't pull in the engine.\n 87 | \n 88 | **Results**\n 89 | - `npm test`: 16 files, 150 passed, 0 failed (93 from T1 + 57 new).\n 90 | - `npm run typecheck`: pass. `npm run lint`: pass. `npm run build`: pass (`/` static, `/api/check` + `/api/extract` dynamic).\n 91 | - Smoke test on `next start`: home HTML has `lang=\"as\"`, the Assamese title and the flagship badge. `/api/check` A → likely_eligible + ready_for_review (4 external checks to verify); B → action_required (`name_land_record` action_required, `name_bank_passbook` possible_match → verify); C → action_required (`doc_death_certificate`).\n 92 | - Live AI check with the real key (fake \"SAMPLE ONLY\" Aadhaar image I drew locally): 200, `{ name: \"Ramesh Kumar Sharma\", dob: \"1975-03-12\", aadhaarLast4: \"4821\" }` from the printed \"1234 5678 4821\". Image input is accepted by the Cline API. With no key: 503 `ai_unavailable`, and the UI switches to manual entry.\n 93 | \n 94 | \n 95 | **Design decisions / deviations (please review)**\n 96 | - **No `export const runtime = \"nodejs\"` in the route files.** Next 16.4 fails the build with \"Route segment config \"runtime\" is not compatible with `nextConfig.cacheComponents`\". Node.js is the default (and the only runtime with cacheComponents), so the routes do run on Node. A comment in each route explains this. Rule 03-stack asks for the export, so please confirm.\n 97 | - **The Cline API wraps the OpenAI body as `{ data: { choices } }`.** `ai.ts` accepts both shapes (tested). Before this fix, every live call fell back to `ai_failed`.\n 98 | - **Environment gotcha:** this shell has an empty `CLINE_MODEL` environment variable. Next does not override an existing env var from `.env.local`, so the server saw no model and returned `ai_unavailable`. It works after `Remove-Item Env:CLINE_MODEL`. Added to techContext.\n 99 | - **Minimum data:** nothing is read from the death certificate or BPL proof (the engine only checks that they are present), so `husbandName` is not collected. The cover sheet shows the masked Aadhaar and no account number.\n100 | - **Empty manual docs:** \"Type it in\" adds the document with empty fields. The engine then counts it as present, and its fields show as \"please verify\"/\"could not read\". I think this is right (\"I have it, I'll type it\"); flagging it in case you prefer the slot to count only once a field is filled.\n101 | - A sample replaces any documents and answers already entered and jumps to \"Check what we read\" (all sample fields are ≥ 0.8 confidence, so nothing is highlighted). The purple \"Demo mode: fake sample documents (A)\" label stays on every step and on the printed sheet.\n102 | - Unanswered questions are allowed; the engine marks them needs_verification (a note under the questions says so).\n103 | \n104 | **Open issues**\n105 | - All new Assamese UI strings in `src/i18n.ts` are drafts and need native-speaker review (Das), like the T1 strings.\n106 | - I did not test the UI in a real phone browser here (no browser automation in this environment). The flow was checked through the built HTML and the APIs; a manual click-through on a phone is recommended before the demo.\n107 | - `tasks/NEXT.md` (Claude's T2 spec), `.cline-runs/index.md` and `run-134715-f3yl.log` were already modified before this run, not by me. They are committed as-is with `git add -A`, per the workflow; I did not edit them.\n108 | \n109 | **Requests for Claude**\n110 | - Confirm dropping `export const runtime = \"nodejs\"` (see above), or say whether to turn off `cacheComponents` instead.\n111 | - Confirm that \"Type it in\" should mark a document as added before any field is filled.\n112 | \n113 | \n114 | ## T3: Cline SDK rule maintenance agent (run-152706-g9km, 2026-10-10)\n115 | Followed `tasks/NEXT.md` (the \"type it in\" fix first, then `tasks/backlog/T3-cline-agent.md`). I wrote tests first for every pure module, the store, the service, the tools and the API.\n116 | \n117 | **PLAN (brief)**\n118 | 1. Fix: a doc counts only once its main field has a value (`MAIN_FIELD`, `isDocAdded`, `countedDocs`), with tests; the UI sends only counted docs.\n119 | 2. Install `@cline/sdk` and read its types in node_modules (findings in techContext). A live probe confirmed tool calling through the Cline API.\n120 | 3. Pure core: rule test cases + runner, built-in regression suites, readable diff, proposal policy (enforced by code), JSON merge patch, notice extraction, log summaries.\n121 | 4. `store.ts` (only DB writer, `node:sqlite`, WAL, transactions) → `rules.ts` (validate → test → save proposed → publish/reject, registry sync).\n122 | 5. `ai.ts` `runToolAgent` (the one model module) + `agents/ruleMaintenance.ts` (5 zod tools, system prompt, event stream).\n123 | 6. Admin API (NDJSON stream) + `/admin` UI; make `/` per-request so published versions show at once; `scripts/agent-smoke.mjs`.\n124 | \n125 | **Fix: \"type it in\"**\n126 | - `src/core/docFields.ts` `MAIN_FIELD` (name; land record → ownerNames; death certificate / BPL proof → null = presence only). `src/core/flow.ts` `isDocAdded`, `countedDocs`. 4 new tests in `flow.test.ts`.\n127 | - `DocsStep.tsx`: a started-but-empty slot is amber with \"Type the name on the next screen to add it\" (new i18n key `docs.toType`, as + en). It doesn't count toward required docs. `KaagazApp.tsx` sends `countedDocs(docs)` to `/api/check` and to the cover sheet, so the engine reports an empty typed-in doc as missing.\n128 | \n129 | **Files created**\n130 | - Pure core (all tested): `src/core/ruleTests.ts`, `schemes/regression.ts` (4 cases per built-in scheme), `ruleDiff.ts`, `ruleDiffView.ts`, `rulePolicy.ts`, `mergePatch.ts`, `notice.ts`, `agentLog.ts`.\n131 | - Server: `src/server/store.ts`, `rules.ts`, `agents/ruleMaintenance.ts`, `adminApi.ts`.\n132 | - Routes (thin, with the runtime comment): `src/app/api/admin/rules/route.ts` (GET), `propose/route.ts` (POST, NDJSON), `[id]/publish/route.ts`, `[id]/reject/route.ts`.\n133 | - UI: `src/app/admin/page.tsx` (server: demo notices from docs/ + history), `AdminApp.tsx`, `AgentLog.tsx`, `ProposalCard.tsx`, `VersionHistory.tsx`.\n134 | - `scripts/agent-smoke.mjs`: a manual live check. It runs both demo notices against a running server; `--publish` also publishes and checks `/api/check` and the home page.\n135 | - Tests: `src/core/{ruleTests,ruleDiff,ruleDiffView,rulePolicy,mergePatch,notice,agentLog}.test.ts`, `schemes/regression.test.ts`, `src/server/{store,rules,aiAgent,adminApi}.test.ts`, `agents/ruleMaintenance.test.ts`. The agent is always mocked (a scripted fake that calls the real tools); no network.\n136 | \n137 | **Files changed**\n138 | - `src/server/ai.ts`: adds `runToolAgent` (Cline SDK `Agent`, `providerId: \"openai-compatible\"`, Cline API base URL, `CLINE_API_KEY`/`CLINE_MODEL`). It loads `@cline/sdk` lazily, logs model / promptVersion / inputHash / toolCalls only, retries once if no tool has run yet, then returns `{ error }`; never throws.\n139 | - `src/server/api.ts`: `/api/check` calls `syncRegistry()` first. `src/app/page.tsx`: the catalog is read per request (`connection()` in `<Suspense>`). `src/core/schemes/index.ts`: exports `compareVersions`.\n140 | - `next.config.ts`: `serverExternalPackages` for the `@cline/*` packages (Turbopack can't bundle `@cline/core`). `vitest.config.mts`: `KAAGAZ_DB_PATH=:memory:`. `.gitignore`: `/data/`. `.env.example`: optional `KAAGAZ_DB_PATH`. `package.json`: `@cline/sdk@^0.0.92`.\n141 | - Memory bank: activeContext, progress, systemPatterns, techContext.\n142 | \n143 | **Results**\n144 | - `npm test`: 29 files, **225 passed, 0 failed** (150 before + 75 new). `npm run typecheck`: pass. `npm run lint`: pass. `npm run build`: pass (`/` and `/admin` partial prerender, admin APIs dynamic).\n145 | - **Live agent check** (`scripts/agent-smoke.mjs --publish`, real Cline API, `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5`, throwaway DB):\n146 |   - IGNOAPS notice → new scheme `nsap-old-age` 1.0.0 in about 58 s (the first attempt timed out after 2 tool calls and the gateway retried). 11 top-level fields added; **5/5 new tests pass** (₹200 central, age 60 ok, age 59 → needs verification (provisional), missing BPL proof → action required, age 85 ok). All provenance is provisional (Vikaspedia is not an official URL). The agent itself flagged that ₹500 for 80+ is only a note and that the upper age limit and office are placeholders.\n147 |   - Orunodoi notice → `orunodoi-3` 2.0.0 → **2.1.0** in about 21 s. Changes: `version` + `benefit.overrides[0]` (2026-10-01 to 2026-10-31, stateTopUp 1500, provisional, sourceUrl null). **4 new + 4 regression tests pass**.\n148 |   - After Publish: `/api/check` orunodoi-3 on 2026-10-15 → 2.1.0, stateTopUp 1500, override true; on 2026-11-15 → 1250, override false. `nsap-old-age` → 200 central. The home page lists the Old Age Pension; `/admin` shows live 2.1.0 / 1.0.0 and the built-in versions in the history.\n149 | \n150 | **Design decisions / deviations (please review)**\n151 | - **`rule_versions` has two extra columns, `notice` and `summary`.** `publish` re-checks the proposal, and the \"verified needs a URL from the notice\" rule needs the notice text; the summary is what the reviewer reads first.\n152 | - **Proposal policy is code, not prompt:** the version must go up; ≥ 3 new tests; `verified` is allowed only if carried over unchanged or if its `sourceUrl` is in the notice. `saveProposal` is refused unless every test passes, and `publish` re-runs everything (so a second proposal for the same version can't go live after the first).\n153 | - **Regression tests** = built-in suites + the tests of every published version, so the October tests protect the next Orunodoi version too.\n154 | - **Merge patch for existing schemes** instead of the whole rule: fewer tokens, faster runs, a smaller chance of the model changing something by accident. New schemes are sent as a full rule.\n155 | - **`createTool` does not validate input** (verified), so each tool `safeParse`s its input and returns `{ error }` to the model.\n156 | - `runToolAgent` lives in `ai.ts` to keep rule 3 (one model module). It retries once **only if no tool has run**, because a second run after tool calls could repeat side effects.\n157 | - `/admin` is English (maintainers, not citizens); the agent's Assamese strings are drafts.\n158 | - The UI shows the IGNOAPS \"new scheme\" diff as one entry per top-level field (11 entries); nested detail is in the formatted values.\n159 | \n160 | **Open issues**\n161 | - **`/admin` has no authentication.** Anyone who can reach the server can run the agent (it costs API credits) and publish rules. Fine for the local demo; must be decided before any deployment.\n162 | - The engine supports one flat benefit amount, so IGNOAPS's ₹500 for 80+ is a note, not computed. The agent also used 120 as an upper age placeholder, because `AgeRange.max` is required.\n163 | - A live run takes about 20–60 s; a model timeout can cost one retry (seen once in the IGNOAPS run).\n164 | - I did not click through `/admin` or `/` in a real browser here (no browser automation). Both were checked through the server-rendered HTML and the APIs on `next start`.\n165 | - `tasks/NEXT.md`, `.cline-runs/index.md` and `.cline-runs/run-144641-b8cr.log` were already modified before this run. I committed them as they are with `git add -A`, per the workflow, and did not edit them.\n166 | \n167 | **Requests for Claude**\n168 | - Decide on `/admin` protection for the demo (e.g. a shared passcode in `.env.local`, or local-only), or confirm none.\n169 | - Should the engine support age-banded benefits (IGNOAPS ₹200 for 60–79, ₹500 for 80+), and should `AgeRange.max` become optional (IGNOAPS has no upper limit)? Both are small schema/engine changes outside T3's scope.\n170 | - Please confirm the two extra `rule_versions` columns (`notice`, `summary`).\n171 | \n172 | ","success":true}],"durationMs":6}}
