{"ts":"2026-10-10T11:29:28.967Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"tool","toolName":"search_codebase","toolCallId":"toolu_019gTUVqG5xZthLULVGiwRc8","output":[{"query":"possible_match.*ok|never.*ok","result":"Found 15 results for pattern: possible_match.*ok|never.*ok\nSearched 135 files.\n\n.clinerules/01-quality.md:8:39\n  6: 4. One writer per piece of state: only the store module touches the database, and only inside transactions.\n  7: 5. Secrets live only in `.env.local` (never committed, never printed, never sent to the browser).\n> 8: 6. Collect the minimum personal data; never collect camera, location, keystroke or emotion data unless the problem statement requires it.\n  9: 7. Keep the app runnable at every commit: `npm test` and `npm run build` pass before you finish a task.\n  10: \n\ndocs/schemes.md:63:4\n  61: Output levels, from strongest to weakest:\n  62: - `same`: identical after formatting normalisation (case, punctuation, extra spaces, joined vs spaced words, honorifics SHRI/SMT/MR/MRS/KUMARI/LATE). → check `ok`.\n> 63: - `possible_match`: differs only by known abbreviations or variants (KR↔KUMAR, MD/MOHD↔MOHAMMAD, DEVI↔DEBI, SK↔SHEIKH), transliteration (Devanagari/Assamese/Bengali script ↔ Latin), or Jaro-Winkler ≥ 0.85 on the normalised form. → `needs_verification`: \"These look like the same person written differently. Officials may still reject this. Ask the bank/Aadhaar centre to make them identical.\"\n  64: - `initials_only`: \"R. KUMAR\" vs \"RAMESH KUMAR\" → `needs_verification`.\n  65: - `mismatch`: below that threshold (e.g. \"Rameshwar Sharma\" vs \"Ramesh Kumar Sharma\", \"Ramesh\" vs \"Suresh\") → `action_required`, saying which document to correct and where.\n\ndocs/schemes.md:66:45\n  64: - `initials_only`: \"R. KUMAR\" vs \"RAMESH KUMAR\" → `needs_verification`.\n  65: - `mismatch`: below that threshold (e.g. \"Rameshwar Sharma\" vs \"Ramesh Kumar Sharma\", \"Ramesh\" vs \"Suresh\") → `action_required`, saying which document to correct and where.\n> 66: - The score is shown for transparency but **never** turns a check into `ok` by itself; only `same` does.\n  67: \n\nmemory-bank/productContext.md:35:22\n  33: - The AI only reads and explains; the rule engine decides.\r\n  34: - Every rule carries provenance; provisional rules and external facts (bank seeding, account active, eKYC, land verified) → needs_verification, never a definitive pass/fail.\r\n> 35: - A fuzzy name score never equals identity: only an exact (normalised) match is `ok`.\r\n  36: - Aadhaar masked to the last 4 digits everywhere; images processed in memory, never stored.\r\n  37: - Demo uses fake sample documents only. AI-generated Assamese is labelled \"draft\"; fixed Assamese strings need native-speaker review.\r\n\nmemory-bank/systemPatterns.md:40:110\n  38: \r\n  39: ## Testing\r\n> 40: Vitest + fast-check, tests first for core logic. Properties: name same-as-itself, symmetry, mask ≤ 4 digits, possible_match never `ok`, Orunodoi never `not_eligible`, evaluate deterministic + schema-valid, readiness invariant.\r\n  41: \n\nmemory-bank/techContext.md:41:76\n  39: - Next 16.4 + `cacheComponents: true` **rejects `export const runtime = \"nodejs\"`** in route files (build error). Node.js is the default runtime, so routes omit it.\r\n  40: - The Cline API (`/chat/completions`) returns the OpenAI body wrapped as `{ data: { choices: [...] } }`. Image input (`image_url` data URL) works with `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5`.\r\n> 41: - This PowerShell session had an **empty `CLINE_MODEL` env var** set. Next never overrides an existing env var from `.env.local`, so the AI looked unconfigured. Run `Remove-Item Env:CLINE_MODEL` before `next dev`/`next start` if `/api/extract` says `ai_unavailable` while `.env.local` is filled.\r\n  42: - In Vitest, `beforeEach(() => mock.mockReset())` returns the mock, which Vitest then runs as a teardown. Use a block body `beforeEach(() => { mock.mockReset(); })`.\r\n  43: - Manual smoke test: `npm run build`, `npx next start -p 3123`, `node scripts/smoke.mjs http://localhost:3123`.\r\n\nsrc/core/evaluate.test.ts:74:76\n  72:   });\r\n  73: \r\n> 74:   it(\"bank name \\\"RAMESH KR SHARMA\\\" → needs_verification (possible match, never ok)\", () => {\r\n  75:     const docs = [aadhaar(\"Ramesh Kumar Sharma\"), passbook(\"RAMESH KR SHARMA\"), land(\"Ramesh Kumar Sharma\")];\r\n  76:     const r = evaluate(pmKisan, docs, pmNo, AS_OF);\r\n\nsrc/core/evaluate.test.ts:351:7\n  349: \r\n  350: describe(\"evaluate: properties\", () => {\r\n> 351:   it(\"possible_match (or anything short of same) never yields an ok check\", () => {\r\n  352:     fc.assert(\r\n  353:       fc.property(nameArb, nameArb, nameArb, (a, b, l) => {\r\n\nsrc/core/evaluate.test.ts:359:45\n  357:         }\r\n  358:         const bank = check(r, \"name_bank_passbook\");\r\n> 359:         return !(nameMatch(a, b).level === \"possible_match\" && bank.result === \"ok\");\r\n  360:       }),\r\n  361:       { numRuns: 500 },\r\n\nsrc/core/evaluate.ts:3:50\n  1: // The deterministic rule engine: evaluate(scheme, docs, answers, asOfDate) → Report. Pure.\r\n  2: // Two verdicts (eligibility, readiness). Provisional rules and external facts never decide; they\r\n> 3: // return needs_verification. A fuzzy name score never becomes `ok`; only `same` does.\r\n  4: import { ageOn } from \"./age\";\r\n  5: import { benefitOn } from \"./benefit\";\r\n\nsrc/core/nameMatch.ts:2:19\n  1: // Defensive name consistency (docs/schemes.md, \"Name consistency\"). Pure.\r\n> 2: // Levels: same > possible_match > initials_only > mismatch. Only `same` may ever become an `ok` check.\r\n  3: import { transliterate } from \"./transliterate\";\r\n  4: import type { NameMatchResult } from \"./types\";\r\n\ntasks/backlog/T1-core-engine.md:22:77\n  20: **Tests (write first):**\n  21: - nameMatch: \"Ramesh Kumar\" vs \"RAMESH KUMAR \" → same; \"RAMESHKUMAR\" vs \"Ramesh Kumar\" → same; \"Smt. Sunita Devi\" vs \"SUNITA DEBI\" → possible_match; \"RAMESH KR SHARMA\" vs \"Ramesh Kumar Sharma\" → possible_match; \"R. Kumar\" vs \"Ramesh Kumar\" → initials_only; \"Rameshwar Sharma\" vs \"Ramesh Kumar Sharma\" → mismatch; \"Ramesh\" vs \"Suresh\" → mismatch.\n> 22: - fast-check: a name is `same` as itself; level is symmetric; `maskAadhaar` never outputs more than 4 digits; **possible_match never yields an `ok` check**.\n  23: - evaluate, PM-KISAN: clean → ready_for_review with bank seeding as needs_verification; bank \"RAMESH KR SHARMA\" → needs_verification; land \"Rameshwar Sharma\" → action_required (fixWhere circle office); missing land_record → action_required; income tax yes → not_eligible; large landholding has NO effect (regression test for the removed 2-ha limit).\n  24: - evaluate, widow: age 39 → not_eligible; 40 → likely_eligible; 79 → likely_eligible; 80 → not_eligible; benefit centralShare 300; stateTopUp null.\n\ntasks/LOG.md:45:125\n  43: \n  44: **Results**\n> 45: - `npm test`: 8 files, **93 passed, 0 failed** (including fast-check properties: same-as-itself, symmetry, mask ≤ 4 digits, possible_match never ok, Orunodoi never not_eligible, deterministic + schema-valid report, readiness invariant).\n  46: - `npm run typecheck`: pass. `npm run lint`: pass. `npm run build`: pass. The built HTML has `lang=\"as\"`, the Assamese title and both taglines, and no Devanagari.\n  47: - Required name cases and their scores: same (1) / same (1) / possible_match (0.999) / possible_match (0.999) / initials_only (0.875) / mismatch (0.644) / mismatch (0.778).\n\ntasks/LOG.md:55:69\n  53: - **Name `same`** means identical after formatting (case, punctuation, spaces, joined words, leading honorifics), compared in the original script. Any cross-script comparison is at best `possible_match`. The score is capped at 0.999 for anything that is not `same`. `possible_match` also covers reordered words and \"every word pair Jaro-Winkler ≥ 0.85\". A missing or extra word is a `mismatch` (so \"Rameshwar Sharma\" vs \"Ramesh Kumar Sharma\" is a mismatch).\n  54: - **Honorifics** are dropped only when they lead the name, so \"Sunita Kumari\" keeps KUMARI as a surname.\n> 55: - **PM-KISAN land owner:** a mismatch becomes `needs_verification` (never ok) if the user answers `land_in_family_member_name` = yes. docs/schemes.md allows \"applicant (or a family member) as owner\". The relationship can't be proven from a photo.\n  56: - **Orunodoi** name checks use the ration card as the reference. Provisional questions are `nfsa_enrolled`, an any-of list and 7 exclusions. \"None of the any-of conditions\" → `needs_verification`. `ration_card_valid` is an external check.\n  57: - **Widow pension** mandatory docs include `bpl_proof`, all provisional (docs/schemes.md: \"commonly required; confirm locally\"). A DOB that is low-confidence, unreadable or missing → age `needs_verification`, never `not_eligible`.\n\ntasks/NEXT.md:12:260\n  10: ## Do, in this order (stop and commit if time runs out)\n  11: 1. **Admin passcode:** an optional env var `ADMIN_PASSCODE` (add it to `.env.example` with no value). If it's set, every `/api/admin/*` route requires the header `x-admin-passcode`, and `/admin` shows a passcode box (kept in sessionStorage). If it's not set, `/admin` shows a visible \"Demo mode: unprotected\" banner. Add tests.\n> 12: 2. **Guardrails audit**, with a test for each where possible: Aadhaar masked in UI, logs and print; no images stored; all AI output zod-validated; disclaimer footer on every report; provenance + \"verified on\" + provisional badge on every check; a fuzzy score never yields `ok`. Fix anything missing. Write the checklist and results into `tasks/LOG.md`.\n  13: 3. **Rejection decoder** `/decode` (small): a textarea (paste a rejection/status message) → `ai.ts` `classifyRejection()` → ONE code from `rejectionCodes.ts` (zod enum) + confidence → fix steps from code (Assamese + English). `UNKNOWN` or confidence < 0.7 → \"needs verification\" + what to ask at the office. Mock the AI in tests. Link it from the home page (\"Got a rejection? Decode it\").\n  14: 4. **`npm run demo:reset`:** clears `data/kaagaz.db` proposals and versions back to the built-in v1 rule packs. Make sure the home page then lists only the 3 original schemes.\n","success":true},{"query":"ageRange|range\\.max|AgeRange","result":"Found 36 results for pattern: ageRange|range\\.max|AgeRange\nSearched 135 files.\n\nmemory-bank/projectbrief.md:44:160\n  42: ## Data model sketch\n  43: - `RuleProvenance` { sourceUrl, sourceTitle, clause?, effectiveDate?, verifiedOn, version, status: verified | provisional }\n> 44: - `SchemeRule` { id, version, nameEn, nameAs, benefit { centralShare, stateTopUp|null, period, effectiveDate, provenance }, mandatoryDocs[], supportingDocs[], ageRange?, eligibilityAnyOf[], exclusions[], externalChecks[], each criterion with provenance }\n  45: - `ExtractedDoc` { docType, fields { name, dob, aadhaarLast4, accountNo, ifsc, ownerNames[], husbandName, ... }, confidence per field }\n  46: - `Report` { eligibility, readiness, checks[], schemeVersion, asOfDate }\n\nsrc/core/evaluate.ts:214:24\n  212: // ---------- eligibility ----------\r\n  213: function ageCheck(scheme: SchemeRule, docs: readonly ExtractedDoc[], asOfDate: string): Check | null {\r\n> 214:   const range = scheme.ageRange;\r\n  215:   if (!range) return null;\r\n  216:   const base = { id: \"age\", kind: \"eligibility\" as const, provenance: range.provenance };\r\n\nsrc/core/evaluate.ts:224:92\n  222:   if (!doc || !dob) {\r\n  223:     return unsure(\r\n> 224:       `We need the date of birth from the ${src.en} to check the age limit (${range.min}–${range.max}).`,\r\n  225:       `বয়সৰ সীমা (${range.min}–${range.max}) পৰীক্ষা কৰিবলৈ ${src.as}ৰ জন্মৰ তাৰিখ লাগিব।`,\r\n  226:     );\r\n\nsrc/core/evaluate.ts:225:35\n  223:     return unsure(\r\n  224:       `We need the date of birth from the ${src.en} to check the age limit (${range.min}–${rang