{"ts":"2026-10-10T11:34:43.302Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"I'm weighing whether the auth guard check should run before or after calling connection(), since the test expects a 401 without needing a full request scope, but connection() is needed for dynamic rendering under cacheComponents.\n\nSeparately, I realize the admin page server component currently fetches scheme history server-side even when passcode protection is enabled, which would leak data before the passcode check — so protected mode should pass an empty initial history and let the client fetch it after authentication.\n\nFor the AdminApp component, I need to manage the passcode via sessionStorage so requests include it as a header, and prompt for entry if protected and missing. To avoid hydration mismatches and satisfy the newer react-hooks lint rule against setting state in effects, I'll use useSyncExternalStore with a server snapshot of empty string, backed by a small sessionStorage-reading store that reacts to storage events.\n\nWhen a passcode is entered, I'll verify it directly by fetching the admin rules endpoint with the header -- storing it and loading history on success, showing a \"wrong passcode\" error on 401, and clearing it on any future 401 response.\n\nI'll build the admin UI next, using sessionStorage with useSyncExternalStore for a hydration-safe passcode flow, showing a passcode prompt when protected and an \"unprotected\" banner otherwise, while ensuring the server page doesn't leak history when protection is on.\n\n"}}
