{"ts":"2026-10-10T11:37:57.916Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"Moving to the guardrails audit now—checking that Aadhaar is masked across UI, logs, and print output, since CoverSheet uses maskAadhaar and the confirm step only shows the last 4 digits. I need to figure out how to test this with Vitest, considering whether it can render the .tsx components properly.\n\nI'm planning to use react-dom/server's renderToStaticMarkup to render CoverSheet, ReportStep, and CheckItem since none of them rely on hooks, which would verify the disclaimer footer appears on every report and that provenance, verification date, and provisional badges show on every check. I'm also flagging a gap: the cover sheet shows provisional status but not per-check provenance or verified-on dates, since that level of detail seems to belong to CheckItem rather than CoverSheet, and I want to keep the scope small.\n\nFor the logging and storage requirements, I'm thinking about adding a test confirming classifyRejection logs don't leak message text, plus a static source-scan test that checks no file outside store.ts uses raw filesystem write APIs and that the database schema has no image column, since mocking fs directly is tricky in ESM.\n\nFor AI output validation, I'm planning a guardrails test file that statically checks only ai.ts references chat/completions or the SDK, alongside tests confirming classifyRejection rejects invalid codes.\n\nI also want to verify every generated report always includes the disclaimer footer and cover sheet, plus confirm each check item displays its verification date, provisional label, and source title—then cross-check that fuzzy matching scores never silently resolve as \"ok\".\n\nFor Aadhaar masking, I'm confirming the ExtractedDoc schema rejects anything other than a 4-digit last-4 value, which locks down the UI and API guarantee together. Next I want to write the test for item 2 and fix the cover sheet, starting with a quick check that vitest handles JSX rendering properly.\n\nFor the report creation test, I'll use the sample scheme data with a fixed as-of date, rendering with react-dom/server's renderToStaticMarkup via createElement rather than JSX to keep the test file plain TypeScript. I'm also checking that the Assamese and English disclaimer text don't contain apostrophes, since renderToStaticMarkup escapes them as HTML entities and that could break string comparisons in the test.\n\nI need a small escaping helper matching React's output rules for ampersands, quotes, and angle brackets, so I can safely compare source titles that might contain special characters, and I'll test both \"as\" and \"en\" language variants. For the cover sheet update, I'm adding the source and verification date fields to the output format string.\n\nItem 1 is complete. Now moving to the guardrails audit — I'll write `src/guardrails.test.ts` to render sample reports and check static rules, and I found that the cover sheet is missing the source and \"verified on\" date, which I'll fix.\n\n"}}
