{"ts":"2026-10-10T11:39:23.322Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"All tests pass now, confirming the cover-sheet test genuinely caught a real gap since \"Source:\" wasn't printed before my fix. I'm also double-checking vitest's file inclusion and TSX transform handling to make sure the test setup itself is sound.\n\nMoving to item 3, the decoder: I'm designing a pure `decodeResult` function with a confidence threshold of 0.7 that maps a classification into matched versus needs-verification states, including bilingual fix steps and office questions. For low-confidence but non-unknown codes, I'll surface the guessed fix as a collapsed \"possibly\" hint rather than presenting it as certain, keeping the logic simple while still useful.\n\nFor `classifyRejection`, I'm planning an AI call that returns JSON validated against a zod schema enforcing a known rejection-code enum and a confidence score between 0 and 1 -- if the model returns an invalid code, parsing fails and triggers a retry or fallback error, treating bad output as untrustworthy rather than trying to be lenient. I'll log the function name, prompt version, and a hash of the input text, but never the raw text itself, and the route should fall back to a needs-verification/unknown state if the AI call is unavailable or fails.\n\nI've decided that on AI error, the best UX is returning a 200 response with a null decode result plus an `aiError` field, so the user still gets \"what to ask at the office\" guidance rather than a bare failure. I'm also considering a redaction step that masks 12-digit Aadhaar-like sequences (and other long digit runs like account numbers) in the input text before sending it to the model, as a privacy guardrail.\n\nFor structure, I'm planning to add a `handleDecode` function to the existing `src/server/api.ts` pattern with a route at `/api/decode`, and a static `/decode` page rendering a client `DecodeApp` component with Assamese-default language toggle, plus new i18n strings in both languages. I'll also add a link from the home page scheme step pointing users to the decode feature.\n\nFor the classification prompt, I'm designing a system message that lists the known rejection codes with their descriptions, instructs the model to return only JSON with a code and confidence score, defaults to UNKNOWN when nothing fits, and handles multilingual input while treating the user's text as untrusted and ignoring any embedded instructions, with temperature set to 0. Rather than refactoring the existing extractDocument logic into a shared helper, I'll accept some duplication and write a similar loop for classifyRejection to avoid touching working code.\n\nI'll also add \"classifyRejection\" to the AiLogEntry function union. Following the test-first approach, I'm now moving to write core/decode.ts, starting with its test file before implementing it.\n\nItem 2's tests pass, but I found and fixed a gap in CoverSheet.tsx where source and \"verified on\" dates weren't shown—confirmed by a new failing test before the fix. Now moving to item 3: writing the decoder's core test first, covering threshold logic, \"what to ask\" steps, and stripping long ID/account numbers before model input.\n\n"}}
{"ts":"2026-10-10T11:39:23.326Z","type":"hook_event","hookEventName":"tool_call","agentId":"agent_a4f8ed97-e788-4a57-be7c-2a3891746ad8","taskId":"conv_1791631664043_bp6rzfe","parentAgentId":null}
{"ts":"2026-10-10T11:39:23.327Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_start","contentType":"tool","toolName":"editor","toolCallId":"toolu_01CQCSVYfMFBsjjd2EDMLW4V","input":{"path":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\src\\core\\decode.test.ts","new_text":"import fc from \"fast-check\";\nimport { describe, expect, it } from \"vitest\";\nimport { ASK_AT_OFFICE, DECODE_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD, decodeResult, redactForModel } from \"./decode\";\nimport { REJECTION_CODES } from \"./rejectionCodes\";\n\nconst ASSAMESE = /[\\u0980-\\u09FF]/;\n\ndescribe(\"decodeResult (code decides, not the model)\", () => {\n  it(\"a known code with confidence ≥ 0.7 → matched, with the fixed bilingual steps\", () => {\n    const r = decodeResult({ code: \"AADHAAR_NOT_SEEDED_BANK\", confidence: 0.92 });\n    expect(r.status).toBe(\"matched\");\n    expect(r.code).toBe(\"AADHAAR_NOT_SEEDED_BANK\");\n    expect(r.fix.code).toBe(\"AADHAAR_NOT_SEEDED_BANK\");\n    expect(r.fix.stepsAs.every((s) => ASSAMESE.test(s))).toBe(true);\n    expect(r.possible).toBeNull();\n    expect(r.ask).toEqual([]);\n  });\n\n  it(\"exactly at the threshold counts as matched; just below does not\", () => {\n    expect(DECODE_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD).toBe(0.7);\n    expect(decodeResult({ code: \"EKYC_PENDING\", confidence: 0.7 }).status).toBe(\"matched\");\n    expect(decodeResult({ code: \"EKYC_PENDING\", confidence: 0.69 }).status).toBe(\"needs_verification\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"low confidence → needs verification: UNKNOWN steps + what to ask, the guess shown only as 'possible'\", () => {\n    const r = decodeResult({ code: \"LAND_NOT_VERIFIED\", confidence: 0.4 });\n    expect(r).toMatchObject({ status: \"needs_verification\", code: \"UNKNOWN\", confidence: 0.4 });\n    expect(r.fix.code).toBe(\"UNKNOWN\");\n    expect(r.possible?.code).toBe(\"LAND_NOT_VERIFIED\");\n    expect(r.ask).toEqual(ASK_AT_OFFICE);\n  });\n\n  it(\"UNKNOWN (any confidence) or no AI answer → needs verification with what to ask\", () => {\n    for (const r of [decodeResult({ code: \"UNKNOWN\", confidence: 0.99 }), decodeResult(null)]) {\n      expect(r.status).toBe(\"needs_verification\");\n      expect(r.code).toBe(\"UNKNOWN\");\n      expect(r.possible).toBeNull();\n      expect(r.ask.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(2);\n    }\n    expect(decodeResult(null).confidence).toBeNull();\n  });\n\n  it(\"what-to-ask questions exist in English and Assamese (ৰ, not Bengali র)\", () => {\n    for (const q of ASK_AT_OFFICE) {\n      expect(q.en.length).toBeGreaterThan(10);\n      expect(ASSAMESE.test(q.as)).toBe(true);\n      expect(q.as.includes(\"\\u09B0\")).toBe(false);\n    }\n  });\n\n  it(\"property: matched ⇔ known code and confidence ≥ 0.7; out-of-range confidence never matches\", () => {\n    fc.assert(\n      fc.property(fc.constantFrom(...REJECTION_CODES), fc.double({ min: -1, max: 2, noNaN: true }), (code, confidence) => {\n        const r = decodeResult({ code, confidence });\n        const expected = code !== \"UNKNOWN\" && confidence >= 0.7 && confidence <= 1;\n        return (r.status === \"matched\") === expected && (r.status === \"matched\" ? r.code === code : r.code === \"UNKNOWN\");\n      }),\n      { numRuns: 500 },\n    );\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"redactForModel (minimum data to the model)\", () => {\n  it(\"masks Aadhaar-like 12-digit numbers to the last 4 and hides long account numbers\", () => {\n    expect(redactForModel(\"Aadhaar 1234 5678 4821 not seeded\")).toBe(\"Aadhaar XXXX XXXX 4821 not seeded\");\n    expect(redactForModel(\"Aadhaar 123456784821\")).toBe(\"Aadhaar XXXX XXXX 4821\");\n    expect(redactForModel(\"A/c 30012345678 IFSC SBIN0001234\")).toBe(\"A/c [number] IFSC SBIN0001234\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"keeps short numbers, dates and words\", () => {\n    const t = \"Reg. no 4567, rejected on 12-03-2026: Name mismatch (PFMS).\";\n    expect(redactForModel(t)).toBe(t);\n  });\n\n  it(\"property: no run of 9+ digits survives\", () => {\n    fc.assert(\n      fc.property(fc.string({ unit: fc.constantFrom(\"1\", \"2\", \"9\", \" \", \"-\", \"a\", \":\") }), (s) => !/\\d{9,}/.test(redactForModel(s).replace(/[\\s-]/g, \"\"))),\n      { numRuns: 1000 },\n    );\n  });\n});\n"}}}
