{"ts":"2026-10-10T11:39:50.077Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"I need to reconsider how numbers are defined for the 9+ digit check—separate short digit groups joined by spaces or dashes could combine into a long run once whitespace is stripped, so the redactor should treat digit sequences separated only by spaces/dashes as part of one logical number when checking length.\n\nA newline between digit groups would also join them since whitespace includes it, but that's fine since being overly cautious is acceptable here. Now I should move on to checking decode.ts in core to confirm it stays pure.\n\n"}}
