{"ts":"2026-10-10T11:45:41.891Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"I'm confirming the script can safely import store.ts directly since Node's type stripping erases the type-only imports, and I can suppress the stray MODULE_TYPELESS warning with a disable-warning flag.\n\nI also realize if a server is already running, its in-memory registry only adds published versions and never removes them, so a running instance would keep listing stale schemes until restarted — I need to either add an unregister mechanism or just document that a restart is required.\n\nTo solve this properly, I'm adding a way to reset the registry back to just the built-in schemes and then comparing it against the currently published versions in syncRegistry, clearing out anything that's been registered at runtime but isn't in the published set anymore, so the registry self-heals rather than requiring a manual restart.\n\nFound a gap: since `syncRegistry` only adds entries, a running server keeps stale agent versions after `demo:reset` until restarted. I'll update it to detect unpublished versions and rebuild from the built-ins.\n\n"}}
