{"ts":"2026-10-10T11:48:18.520Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"All the live smoke results look good, and the live API example returns AADHAAR_NOT_SEEDED_BANK with 0.98 confidence while logs only store the hash. I'm also checking whether the /admin locked mode renders the passcode box correctly given the SSR behavior with useSyncExternalStore defaulting to locked on the server—it seems fine since PasscodeBox still renders in SSR.\n\nI'm verifying the unprotected banner is correctly set to false, so I'm moving on. For item 5, I'm time-boxing the polish work—doing a minimal check for fixed widths that could overflow at 360px rather than a full pass, since the components already use flex-wrap and the decode app has loading states; I'll just note this as minimal/not done in the log.\n\nI'm deciding to skip the optional AgeRange.max change since it touches engine messages, types, and tests with real risk, and we're already around 50 minutes in—I'll record it as future scope instead, along with age-based payment bands. I also need to mention the backup path for the demo database rows I cleared during reset, and then append the guardrails info to LOG.md.\n\nNow I'm planning the final steps: writing the LOG.md entry with a timestamp, updating the memory bank files (activeContext, progress, and small edits to techContext/systemPatterns), confirming the guardrails test regex only expects the passcode storage path, and then rerunning lint, typecheck, and tests since lint hasn't been run since the item 4 changes.\n\nAll live checks pass, including a real Cline API call returning the expected classification with Assamese steps and hashed logs. Given the time budget, I'll limit item 5 to a layout check, skip the `AgeRange.max` change (too large a scope), and move on to running final lint/typecheck/test gates before writing the log and memory bank.\n\n"}}
