{"ts":"2026-10-10T11:49:00.105Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"Items 1-4 are done and passing, about 21 minutes elapsed so far. Now I'm on item 5, small polish items like a 360px check and loading states, plus the optional AgeRange.max if time allows. I also noticed docs/README-draft.md appeared unexpectedly, not something I created, so I'll commit it along with everything else and flag it as a note. For the 360px check, I don't have browser access so I need another approach.\n\nReviewing the layouts without a live browser, the flex structures on the decode, home, and admin pages look reasonable, and loading states already exist in most places except the home page's Suspense fallback, which just shows an ellipsis. I'll make a cheap improvement there with a bilingual loading text, while leaving things like text wrapping alone since they already handle long strings fine. The optional AgeRange.max change looks like it would touch the evaluate messages, agent schema, and flow logic, likely pushing past the 10-minute budget, so I'll skip it and just note it in the log. Plan is to do the small fallback fix, then write the log, update the memory bank, add a \"Future scope\" note about age-based payment bands in progress.md, and commit everything.\n\nTests, typecheck, lint, build, and smoke runs all pass — I'm 21 minutes into the 60-minute box. I'll add a quick loading fallback for `/`, skip the optional `AgeRange.max` change since it's too large for the remaining time, then write the log, update the memory bank, and commit.\n\n"}}
